00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.926
When you're making a movie centered around dreams, you're going to spend

00:00:22.948 --> 00:00:23.978
a lot of time in bedrooms.

00:00:24.074 --> 00:00:27.318
A Nightmare on Elm Street gets it right, making each location feel like a

00:00:27.324 --> 00:00:28.342
real teenager's room.

00:00:28.396 --> 00:00:31.814
But if you look closely, you start to notice one element that repeats over

00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:35.440
and over... birds. Why are there so many birds? 

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.506
As I've discussed in the past, when director

00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:40.998
Wes Craven wasn't brewing up nightmares, he spent his free time bird watching.

00:00:40.998 --> 00:00:44.326
Scream 2022 made an homage to Craven by putting the sound of bird calls

00:00:44.358 --> 00:00:47.430
under his memoriam and filling the house with bird artwork.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.854
In A Nightmare on Elm Street,

00:00:48.902 --> 00:00:50.890
there's a goose statue in Tina's living room.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.598
Her mom's room has peacock silhouettes and a swan and pigeon ornament on the shelves. 

00:00:54.624 --> 00:00:57.786
Nancy's kitchen contains a chicken on the wall and a rooster above

00:00:57.818 --> 00:00:58.330
the fridge.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.765
Glen's room has a lot of weird stuff, including this picture of three baby chicks

00:01:02.765 --> 00:01:04.430
with Nancy's name on it.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.338
Did she paint this for him or did he paint it in honor of her, then hang it

00:01:08.344 --> 00:01:11.454
up in his room? Glen's mom can also be seen holding a newspaper.

00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:14.258
The headline reads Birds get names, but only three.

00:01:14.344 --> 00:01:17.346
This seems to be related to Craven's hobby, because a bird watcher will

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:20.098
usually try to identify or name the birds that he spots.

00:01:20.194 --> 00:01:23.826
Finally, and perhaps most ominously, is the toy vulture perched on Glen's bed,

00:01:23.858 --> 00:01:27.158
a species of bird known for feasting on the remains of the dead, which

00:01:27.164 --> 00:01:29.053
is what Glen is about to become. 

00:01:29.053 --> 00:01:32.625
Like a bird, the nightmare that Wes Craven crafted on the silver screen

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.467
would take flight as one of the iconic slashers of all time.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.666
